<header class="sg-head"><p class="featured-region">Dance · 1860 · Europe</p><h1 class="sg-title">Kalinka</h1><p class="sg-local"><bdi lang="ru">Калинка</bdi> / <bdi lang="ru-Latn">Kalinka</bdi></p><p class="sg-kid" data-say>A fast, cheerful Russian song from 1860, named after the snowball tree, that speeds up each time its chorus comes round.</p></header>
<dl class="sg-facts"><div><dt>Words</dt><dd>Ivan Larionov</dd></div><div><dt>Music</dt><dd>Ivan Larionov</dd></div><div><dt>Culture</dt><dd>Russians</dd></div><div><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian</dd></div><div><dt>Place</dt><dd>Saratov, Russia</dd></div><div><dt>Date</dt><dd>1860</dd></div><div><dt>Type</dt><dd>Dance</dd></div><div><dt>The words</dt><dd>Public domain (words and music by Ivan Larionov (1860))</dd></div></dl>
<div class="sg-body">
<section class="sg-sec" id="story"><h2>The story</h2><p>&quot;Kalinka&quot; is a song in the Russian folk style, written in 1860 by the composer and folklorist Ivan Larionov. It was first performed in Saratov as part of a theatrical entertainment he had composed, and was soon taken into the repertoire of a folk choral group. Its title is the kalinka, the snowball tree (Viburnum opulus).</p><p>The Russian bass Feodor Chaliapin sang it and recorded it in the early days of recording, for His Master's Voice and Victor. Since the end of World War II it has been made known above all by the Alexandrov Ensemble, the official army choir of the Russian Armed Forces, whose arrangement turned the light song into something close to an operatic aria. Pyotr Tverdokhlebov was the first of the ensemble's soloists to sing it. At the Berlin peace concert of August 1948 Viktor Nikitin sang three encores of it and became the first &quot;Mr. Kalinka&quot;, an unofficial title that audiences and journalists give to the soloist of a concert where the song wins many encores. Evgeny Belyaev (1926–1994), one of its best-known singers, earned the title at the ensemble's London concerts of 1956 and 1963, and in 1963 made a definitive recording of it at the Abbey Road Studios in London with the Alexandrov Ensemble under Boris Alexandrovich Alexandrov. Later holders of the title include Vasily Ivanovich Shtefutsa and Vadim Petrovich Ananyev.</p><p>The song is counted among the most famous Russian folk and folk-style songs, in Russia and around the world. The Italian-American bass Ezio Pinza sang it in the 1953 film Tonight We Sing, a semi-biography of Chaliapin. It became one of the theme tunes of Atari's 1988 version of Tetris and has often appeared in licensed Tetris games since, beside &quot;Korobeiniki&quot; and &quot;Troika&quot;. It is the theme of the Russian civilisation in the video game Civilization VI (2016), and the soprano Aida Garifullina sang it at the closing ceremony of the 2018 FIFA World Cup in Russia, with the former footballer Ronaldinho.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="meaning"><h2>What it says</h2><p>A light-hearted song whose refrain calls out to the kalinka, the snowball tree. It is fast, and the refrain quickens each time it returns.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="words"><h2>The words</h2><div class="sg-show" role="group" aria-label="Show these columns"><button type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-col="orig">Russian</button><button type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-col="rom">Romanized</button><button type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-col="en">In English</button></div><div class="sg-blocks"><div class="sg-lyrics sg-cols-3"><div class="sg-colhead" aria-hidden="true"><span class="sg-o">Russian</span><span class="sg-r">Romanized</span><span class="sg-e">In English</span></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="ru">Калинка, калинка, калинка моя!</span><span class="sg-r" lang="ru-Latn">Kalinka, kalinka, kalinka moja!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Little guelder rose, little guelder rose, my little guelder rose!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="ru">В саду ягода малинка, малинка моя!</span><span class="sg-r" lang="ru-Latn">V sadu jagoda malinka, malinka moja!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>In the garden a berry, a little raspberry, my little raspberry!</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="ru">Ах, под сосною, под зеленою,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="ru-Latn">Ax, pod sosnoju, pod zelenoju,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Ah, under the pine, under the green one,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="ru">Спать положите вы меня!</span><span class="sg-r" lang="ru-Latn">Spatʹ položite vy menja!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Lay me down to sleep!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="ru">Ай-люли, люли, ай-люли, люли,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="ru-Latn">Aj-ljuli, ljuli, aj-ljuli, ljuli,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Ai-liuli, liuli, ai-liuli, liuli,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="ru">Спать положите вы меня.</span><span class="sg-r" lang="ru-Latn">Spatʹ položite vy menja.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Lay me down to sleep.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="ru">Калинка, калинка, калинка моя!</span><span class="sg-r" lang="ru-Latn">Kalinka, kalinka, kalinka moja!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Little guelder rose, little guelder rose, my little guelder rose!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="ru">В саду ягода малинка, малинка моя!</span><span class="sg-r" lang="ru-Latn">V sadu jagoda malinka, malinka moja!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>In the garden a berry, a little raspberry, my little raspberry!</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="ru">Ах, сосёнушка, ты зеленая,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="ru-Latn">Ax, sosënuška, ty zelenaja,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Ah, little pine tree, you green one,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="ru">Не шуми ты надо мной!</span><span class="sg-r" lang="ru-Latn">Ne šumi ty nado mnoj!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Do not rustle above me!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="ru">Ай-люли, люли, ай-люли, люли,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="ru-Latn">Aj-ljuli, ljuli, aj-ljuli, ljuli,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Ai-liuli, liuli, ai-liuli, liuli,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="ru">Не шуми ты надо мной!</span><span class="sg-r" lang="ru-Latn">Ne šumi ty nado mnoj!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Do not rustle above me!</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="ru">Калинка, калинка, калинка моя!</span><span class="sg-r" lang="ru-Latn">Kalinka, kalinka, kalinka moja!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Little guelder rose, little guelder rose, my little guelder rose!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="ru">В саду ягода малинка, малинка моя!</span><span class="sg-r" lang="ru-Latn">V sadu jagoda malinka, malinka moja!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>In the garden a berry, a little raspberry, my little raspberry!</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="ru">Ах, красавица, душа-девица,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="ru-Latn">Ax, krasavica, duša-devica,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Ah, beauty, sweetheart maiden,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="ru">Полюби же ты меня!</span><span class="sg-r" lang="ru-Latn">Poljubi že ty menja!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Do love me!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="ru">Ай-люли, люли, ай-люли, люли,</span><span class="sg-r" lang="ru-Latn">Aj-ljuli, ljuli, aj-ljuli, ljuli,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Ai-liuli, liuli, ai-liuli, liuli,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="ru">Полюби же ты меня!</span><span class="sg-r" lang="ru-Latn">Poljubi že ty menja!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Do love me!</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="ru">Калинка, калинка, калинка моя!</span><span class="sg-r" lang="ru-Latn">Kalinka, kalinka, kalinka moja!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Little guelder rose, little guelder rose, my little guelder rose!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="ru">В саду ягода малинка, малинка моя!</span><span class="sg-r" lang="ru-Latn">V sadu jagoda malinka, malinka moja!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>In the garden a berry, a little raspberry, my little raspberry!</span></p></div></div></div><div class="sg-credit"><p>Original: Ivan Larionov (1860); the Russian text as quoted in Wikipedia's article. Text from <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalinka_(1860_song)" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikipedia</a>; public domain.</p><p>The romanization is the Institute&#8217;s own (scientific transliteration).</p><p>The English is the Institute&#8217;s own translation, made from the original for this page.</p></div><details class="sg-notes"><summary>Notes on the translation (4)</summary><ul><li>Romanization: х is written x, ь ʹ, ё ë, й j.</li><li>line 1.1: 'калинка' is a diminutive of 'калина', the guelder rose (snowball tree) and its red berries; 'малинка' a diminutive of 'малина', raspberry. Both are terms of endearment.</li><li>line 2.3: 'ай-люли, люли' are lullaby syllables with no meaning.</li><li>line 6.1: 'душа-девица', literally 'soul-maiden', a fond address.</li></ul></details></section>
</div>
